<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">dollmaster</ansi>

The Doll Master fights through a wooden doll. The Master stays behind with
a dagger and a rod; the doll stands in front and does the striking. The
doll is the Master's whole turn, so a Doll Master company has six bodies
but only five turns. The doll never dodges, but it takes blows in the Master's
place and breaks instead of dying. It is a neutral class: it has no
alignment gate to meet.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Doll Master is</ansi>

  Health      1 to start, 0.55 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 0.7 and Evasion 0.8 a level (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        light armor, no shield, daggers, rods and staffs (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>)
  Stats       smarts 4, perception 3, speed 2, mysticism 1 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starts with the Puppetry skill, which its abilities draw on
  Starter kit a dagger, a cap, a shirt, boots, food, a waterskin, a knapsack and
              doll parts

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The doll</ansi>

  Where       it stands in the formation for a battle and takes no company slot
              (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>); it is gone when the battle ends
  Health      70% of a warrior's at the Master's level
  Attack      90% of the Master's level; it never dodges (Evasion 0)
  Gear        its own weapon (a cudgel to start) and armor, put on with
              <ansi fg="command">doll wield</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">doll wear</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help doll</ansi>)
  Breaking    at 0 health it breaks and is out of the battle, never lost: its
              gear stays on it and it comes back mended
  Persistence it is saved on the Master: name, wear, gear and breaks survive
              a restart
  No mana, no food, no experience: a doll isn't a person

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Doll Master fights</ansi>

Its abilities need no command and use no mana (<ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>):

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Puppet Strike</ansi>     the doll strikes in its Master's place on every turn the Master
                  has, at the foe the Master aims at (or one the front row puts
                  in the way). The Master does not swing. With no doll able to
                  act (broken, stunned or on the ground) the Master swings
                  itself.
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Guard String</ansi>      from level 5, the doll steps in and takes a blow meant for the
                  most hurt ally beside it: twice a battle, three times from
                  level 8.
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Tangle</ansi>            from level 12, strings snag the foe the doll strikes and push its
                  action meter back by half a turn (a quarter for a boss). At
                  most once every 3 rounds, and the same foe can't be tangled
                  again for 2 rounds.
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Emergency Splice</ansi>  from level 18, once a battle a doll that would break stands back
                  up at 25% health, and its Master loses its next turn.

Each blow is a real blow: it can miss, be dodged, blocked or parried, and a
foe it wounds can lose a chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>). A doll that is stunned or knocked
down loses its strike, as any fighter does (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>). Turn abilities off
with <ansi fg="command">strategy [member] abilities off</ansi>.

A doll has no will of its own: if its Master falls, its strings go slack and
it goes limp and leaves the battle, even if it was standing.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Mending</ansi>

Doll parts mend dolls. Each part mends a doll for 10 health plus 3 for each
level of its Master, broken dolls first. The end of a camp rest mends the
company's dolls with the leader's parts (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>), or use <ansi fg="command">doll mend</ansi>
out of battle. Doll parts are sold in Dunmar's market and never bought back.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Routes</ansi>

At level 10 a Doll Master promotes to a Puppeteer, a Golemancer or a
Marionettist. All three are open at any alignment (<ansi fg="command">help dollmaster-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Companions</ansi>

A Doll Master companion fights the same way, with a doll of its own that stands
in front of it. Recruits are hired like any other (<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>); <ansi fg="command">doll [member]</ansi> shows its
doll. Put the Master in the back row and leave the front of its column free.

Commands: <ansi fg="command">doll</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dollmaster-routes</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help doll</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dollmaster-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
